1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,200
Hi everyone, welcome to the show,
this is the first episode

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,800
I started this podcast to talk about
starting a small business

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,199
I had no money, no plan, just a small
idea and questions

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,000
The first thing I learned was that
customers pay for a clear result

5
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:16,400
Most people wait for permission
before they start

6
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,800
I kept my day job for a year while I
tested the idea

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,500
I talked to ten shop owners and asked
what they would pay for

8
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,900
One of them said, just solve one
small problem really well

9
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:30,000
My first sale was only twelve
dollars, but it proved a point

10
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:32,499
I remember thinking, okay, this could
actually become a real business

11
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:33,799
Then I raised the price a little and
nobody complained at all

12
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,200
Pricing was the hardest part, I kept
charging too little

13
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:41,900
The lesson is simple, start small,
charge fairly, and keep going

14
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:45,400
Today I run a tiny team of three and
we serve customers in five cities

15
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:48,800
We still make mistakes every week but
we fix them fast

16
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,300
I want this show to share the real
numbers and costs

17
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,800
Next week I will bring in a guest who
sells soap at markets

18
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,200
She started with fifty dollars and
now she sells out every week

19
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:02,600
If you are starting out too, send me
one question

20
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:06,000
Thanks for listening, and see you
next week, same time

